  "result": "The gate's final verdict is **VACUOUS**, and the cause is in the node and the run's reading, not in the rule or the witnesses. All eight witnesses give their expected verdicts; the only failure is that the commercial-vehicle and taxicab exception memberships are never exercised.\n\n**What I wrote**\n- **Rule:** applies when the vehicle occupies a yellow curb zone, unless one of the two exceptions holds. Each exception is the membership (commercial vehicle, or taxicab) together with a parking-restricted zone sign that governs a lane the subject occupies and whose posted conditions hold for it. The obligation is that the vehicle does not halt, using `p.halt_speed_tolerance`. I made no readings beyond the record's.\n- **Witnesses:** the six planned ones, plus two I added:\n  - `branch_3`: the sign governs the lane across the street.\n  - `branch_4`: a school zone sign whose conditions hold.\n\n  Both added witnesses expect violated. Together they exercise the sign-kind, governs and occupancy leaves.\n\n**Why it can't pass as planned:** in this run's reading, neither `commercial_vehicle` nor `taxicab` includes any road-user class, and every vehicle class is left unresolved for both. So for any vehicle the membership is always unknown. Under three-valued logic, a leaf that is unknown in every scene can never change a decided verdict. The only scenes where it would matter, where the sign's conditions hold, come out unknown, and the rules don't allow a branch witness that expects unknown. No change to the rule or the scenes can fix this.\n\n**Fix for the plan or reading agent (spans s4 and s6):**\n- **Preferred:** mark at least one class as included in each aggregate where the definition's words allow it, for example `ru.commercial_motor_vehicle` under commercial vehicle and `ru.taxicab` under taxicab.\n- **Otherwise:** withdraw the two exceptions as a gap.\n\n**Gate runs:** I used 2 of 6.\n- I wasted one by running the gate on the untouched skeleton.\n- Before that, I also tried the gate command with `--help` and a pipe, which the sandbox denied. It didn't run and didn't use a gate run.\n\nThe full report is in `task_result.md` in the working directory.",
